            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marsha B"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great recipe! my family makes this dish in the fall every year. My mom-mom cooks bacon with the apples though and she adds a touch of brown sugar. Everyone loves it!!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carrie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We loved this! Cooked in a bit of bacon grease, and added 2 slices crumbled bacon near the end, plus about 1/2 tsp brown sugar, which really took them over the top! I peeled the apples for one of my picky eaters and cut the onions into larger pieces for the other - the longer onion strings caramelized nicely with the extra cooking time, and the whole thing tasted great! Served with potato pancakes and sausage with red cabbage. Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2018-03-02T15:02:45.857Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Glenda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Although I do love sweet things, this is a very nice change of pace for something \"apple\". I fried a little bacon, and used part of the grease this produced to sautee the apple and onions, instead of adding butter. When cooked, I seasoned with salt, pepper, and just a light sprinkle of seasoning salt I served this over a little cooked barley for supper, saving a little for the next day to eat as a salad with just a tad of my favorite bleu cheede dressing. Both were unique and tasty. I'm very happy to have found this recipe. Thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-17T13:05:56.107Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Scaled this down to 2 servings and used Gala and Granny Smith apples. Most cooked apple dishes are sweet, so this is a really nice change for a savory side dish which was served warm with a pork entree. Next time I make this, I will add some crumbled crisp bacon as suggested by the recipe author, as that should only enhance its savoriness. Thanks Jin for sharing your recipe, this is a good one!",
            "datePublished": "2013-10-06T12:21:37.570Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Moon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this! My husband is allergic to red onions so I used a Vidalia onion instead. So yummy!",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-07T13:56:46.677Z"
          },
